Task: Extend PaymentStore.update to write the outbox atomically (ADR 0008 / TD-3.4)

Summary: PaymentStore.update now wraps its status-change UPDATE in an
explicit session.transaction. When the update succeeds AND the new status
is Settled, it also INSERTs a matching outbox_events row (aggregate_id =
orderId, correlation_id = orderId, payload = the full EventEnvelope JSON
wrapping a PaymentSettledEvent) in the same transaction. Added
skunk-circe as a new dependency for a proper Codec[Json] against the
jsonb column (avoids a text/jsonb OID mismatch). trace_parent is left
NULL for now - no trace-context extraction exists anywhere in this
codebase yet (that's purekafka/ADR 0010's job, sequenced after this
track).

Deviation from plan.md's literal wording: the plan anticipated needing
'orderId + envelope-building inputs threaded in as new parameters' on
update's signature. Turned out unnecessary - orderId/amountCents/updatedAt
are all already returned by the existing UPDATE...RETURNING clause, so no
new parameters were needed; update(id, status) keeps its original
signature. Same approach, simpler implementation.

Added 3 new PaymentStorePostgresSuite tests (Testcontainers-Postgres):
Settled writes a matching outbox row; non-Settled writes none; unknown id
writes none. Found and fixed a test-isolation issue along the way:
TestContainerForAll shares one Postgres container across the whole test
file, and every existing test in this file reuses the same hardcoded
orderId - so a naive 'assert outbox_events is empty' check in a later
test picks up an earlier test's row. Fixed by filtering outbox rows by
the specific paymentId embedded in each row's own payload instead of
asserting the whole table is empty.

